    "updated_at": "2017-10-31T12:10:16Z",
    "body": "With such a change if we encounter a`<frameset>` in a `<template>` it will implicitly close the `<template>` and detach all nodes from the document up to the `<html>` element which doesn't feels right. It will be surprising and even concerning from the security perspective that `<template>` content can modify ambient AST in such a manner. \r\n\r\nBTW, how we determine which elements modify `frameset-ok` flag? From quick search in W3C mail archive it seems like it was just back-ported from IE.",
