    "body": "Right, frameset in template needs to be ignored.\r\n\r\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=5471\r\n\r\nHow do browsers do this? Do they reset the flag for `</template>` \"in head\"? Or use more insertion modes instead of a flag?\r\n\r\nIIRC, `frameset-ok` was indeed modeled after mostly IE's behavior.",
